// selfhost/typeck/lib.mty
//
// v0.8 scaffolding for the self-hosted type-inference package.
//
// The runnable typeck lives in `infer.mty` as a single consolidated
// module — the v0.8 `mty check` driver still compiles one `.mty` file
// at a time, same single-file constraint as the v0.4 lexer, v0.6
// parser, and v0.8 HIR. This file documents the intended v0.9+ module
// layout once `mty-pkg` lands cross-file module resolution.
//
// ## v0.9+ module layout
//
//   selfhost/typeck/
//     lib.mty           // this file — package root + public re-exports
//     ty.mty            // resolved type representation (Ty, TyId, ...)
//     infer.mty         // bidirectional HM-style inference driver
//     unify.mty         // substitution + unify (post-1.0)
//     items.mty         // item-level type collection (fn sigs first)
//     exprs.mty         // expression-level inference
//     prelude.mty       // built-in type bindings (I32, F64, Str, ...)
//
// ## Public surface
//
// The exported entry point is `infer_package()`, which walks the HIR
// emitted by selfhost_hir through the host bridge and records inferred
// types per binding.
//
//   pub fn infer_package() -> Unit
//
// The bootstrap test in crates/mty-driver/tests/selfhost_typeck.rs
// installs a SelfhostTypeckHost that:
//   1. seeds the HIR from the trusted Rust lowering pipeline
//   2. responds to HIR navigation queries
//   3. captures the per-binding inferred-type event stream
//   4. compares the binding -> type map against the Rust typeck pipeline

package selfhost_typeck_lib
